# Design system

`design-system/` is the visual SSOT. App CSS consumes tokens; it does not reinvent them. Source: `design-system/tokens/design-tokens.json` → `design-system/css/tokens.css`. Rationale: `design-system/docs/DESIGN.md`.

## Tokens to use

- **Surfaces:** `--surface-canvas` (bone), `--surface-card` (paper), `--surface-inverted` (obsidian), `--surface-action` (highlighter).
- **Ink:** `--color-ink` primary text, `--color-ash` secondary, `--color-hairline` / `--color-smoke` borders. Cards elevate with 1px hairline, not drop shadows.
- **Type:** `--font-lausanne` (Inter fallback), weight 400 only. Hierarchy is size + tracking, not weight. Use `--text-*` / `--leading-*` scale.
- **Space:** 4px base; named `--spacing-8` … `--spacing-64`. Round to the scale — no `13px` padding.
- **Radius:** `--radius-buttons` 6px, `--radius-inputs` 10px, `--radius-cards` 16px.

## Highlighter is scarce

`--color-highlighter-yellow` / `--surface-action` marks money-moving or primary action only. Do not tint links, chips, or status with it. Status uses semantic meaning (review needed / trusted / failed) without consuming the brand accent.

## SSOT for repeating visuals

One card treatment, one status-pill treatment, one empty-state treatment. If two screens show "needs review," they share a component or a documented class string. Do not fork a local copy that will drift.

## Anti-patterns

Hardcoded `#e4f222` or `#0c0a08` in app CSS. `font-weight: 700`. New typeface. Box shadows for elevation. Arbitrary spacing (`padding: 13px`). A second token file beside `design-tokens.json`.
